s an arithmetic average of the i -th digit of Masha's number and the i ΓÇë-ΓÇë1 -th digit of her true love's number. If needed, the digit can be rounded up or down. For example, Masha can get: \n 12345 95444 Unfortunately, when Masha tried dialing the number, she got disappointed: as it turned out, the number was unavailable or outside the coverage area. But Masha won't give up. Perhaps, she rounded to a wrong digit or chose the first digit badly. That's why she keeps finding more and more new numbers and calling them. Count the number of numbers Masha calls. Masha calls all the possible numbers that can be found by the described means of arithmancy, except for, perhaps, her own one.\n\n## Input\n\nThe first line contains nonempty sequence consisting of digits from 0 to 9 ΓÇö Masha's phone number. The sequence length does not exceed 50 .\n\n## Output\n\nOutput the single number ΓÇö the number of phone numbers Masha will dial.\n\n## Examples\n\nExample 1:\n```\n12345\n```\n```\n48\n```","type":"text"}],"contestId":44,"index":"H","memoryLimit":"256 megabytes","name":"Phone Number","problemKey":"44-H","rating":null,"tags":[],"timeLimit":"2 seconds","url":"https://codeforces.com/contest/44/problem/H"},{"approaches":[{"label":"Approach 1","number":1,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 2","number":2,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 3","number":3,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 4","number":4,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 5","number":5,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 6","number":6,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 7","number":7,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.cpp","language":"cpp"}]},{"label":"Approach 8","number":8,"solutions":[{"code":"","fileName":"main.c